<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<GameProfile xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
	<GamePath></GamePath>
	<ExecutableName>ago.exe</ExecutableName>
	<ExecutableName2></ExecutableName2>
	<HasTwoExecutables>false</HasTwoExecutables>
	<TestMenuParameter></TestMenuParameter>
	<TestMenuIsExecutable>false</TestMenuIsExecutable>
	<ExtraParameters></ExtraParameters>
	<TestMenuExtraParameters></TestMenuExtraParameters>
	<EmulationProfile>ALLSFGO</EmulationProfile>
	<GameProfileRevision>17</GameProfileRevision>
	<Is64Bit>true</Is64Bit>
	<HasSeparateTestMode>false</HasSeparateTestMode>
	<EmulatorType>TeknoParrot</EmulatorType>
	<Patreon>false</Patreon>
	<DevOnly>false</DevOnly>
	<OnlineIdFieldName>OnlineId</OnlineIdFieldName>
	<OnlineIdType>SegaId</OnlineIdType>
	<ConfigValues>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Input API</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>DirectInput</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>DirectInput</string>
				<string>XInput</string>
			</FieldOptions>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>OnlineID</FieldName>
			<FieldValue></FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Text</FieldType>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Card Menu Key</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0x71</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>KeyCapture</FieldType>
			<Hint>Opens the card picker over the game (default F2): every card you have printed, with its picture. Click a card to put it in the card reader or take it out; the cabinet's deck holds only so many. Cards are kept in TeknoParrot\cards beside the game, each picture carries its card, so a picture alone can be copied to another PC.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>FreePlay</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>1</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>DisplayMode</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>Fullscreen Windowed</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>Windowed</string>
				<string>Fullscreen</string>
				<string>Fullscreen Windowed</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>Windowed: a window of the Resolution's size (smaller if it does not fit the screen). Fullscreen: the monitor switches to the Resolution while the game runs (exclusive). Fullscreen Windowed: a borderless window over the whole monitor, the picture scaled to fill it.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Hide Cursor</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>Hides the mouse cursor over the game, as on the cabinet's touch screen. Leave it off to play with a mouse: the cursor then stays visible, also in full screen.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Resolution</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>1920x1080</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Dropdown</FieldType>
			<FieldOptions>
				<string>1920x1080</string>
				<string>2560x1440</string>
				<string>3200x1800</string>
				<string>3840x2160</string>
				<string>Custom</string>
			</FieldOptions>
			<Hint>The size the game draws its picture at: 1920x1080 is the cabinet's. Larger sizes draw the 3D and the menus sharper, in the same layout; the picture is then scaled to the window or screen, so a size larger than your monitor works as supersampling. Custom: the size in Custom Resolution.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Custom Resolution</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>2880x1620</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Text</FieldType>
			<Hint>Width x height, used when Resolution is Custom, for example 2880x1620. The game's picture is 16:9: another shape is narrowed to the largest 16:9 size inside it. From 1920x1080 up to 7680x4320.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Emulated Daemon</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>1</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
			<Hint>Enable to have TP emulate amdaemon, in that case only the game .exe is needed.</Hint>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Use Keyboard/Button For Axis</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>0</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Bool</FieldType>
		</FieldInformation>
		<FieldInformation>
			<CategoryName>General</CategoryName>
			<FieldName>Keyboard/Button Axis X/Y Sensitivity</FieldName>
			<FieldValue>10</FieldValue>
			<FieldType>Slider</FieldType>
			<FieldMin>1</FieldMin>
			<FieldMax>127</FieldMax>
			<FieldOptions></FieldOptions>
		</FieldInformation>
	</ConfigValues>
